    "block.base.cooked_marlin": "Cooked Marlin",
    "block.base.raw_deepwater_lanternfish": "Raw Deepwater Lanternfish",
    "block.base.cooked_deepwater_lanternfish": "Cooked Deepwater Lanternfish",
    "block.base.raw_swordfish": "Raw Swordfish",
    "block.base.cooked_swordfish": "Cooked Swordfish",
    "block.base.raw_glimmer_koi": "Raw Glimmer Koi",
    "block.base.cooked_glimmer_koi": "Cooked Glimmer Koi",
    "block.base.fishing_rod": "Fishing Rod",
    "block.base.fine_rod": "Fine Rod",
    "block.base.twine": "Twine",
    "block.base.charcoal": "Charcoal",
    "block.base.herb_pouch": "Herb Pouch",
    "block.base.seed_pouch": "Seed Pouch",
    "block.base.grave_ward_amulet": "Grave Ward Amulet",
    "block.base.crafting_table": "Crafting Table",
    "block.base.herb_planter": "Herb Planter",
    "block.base.hay_bale": "Hay Bale",
    "block.base.barrel": "Barrel",
    "block.base.crate": "Crate",
    "block.base.sack": "Sack",
    "block.base.bell": "Bell",
    "block.base.fishing_net": "Fishing Net",
    "block.base.hanging_herbs": "Hanging Herbs",
    "block.base.hearthstone": "Hearthstone",
    "block.base.chimney": "Chimney",
    "block.base.windroot": "Windroot",
    "block.base.coin_purse": "Coin Purse",
    "block.base.stone_altar": "Stone Altar",
    "block.base.gold_coin": "Gold Coin",
    "block.base.fur": "Fur",
    "block.base.fired_clay": "Fired Clay",
    "block.base.flint": "Flint",
    "quest.age.nomad": "Nomad",
    "quest.age.farm": "Farm",
    "quest.base.a_bed_of_your_own": "A Bed of Your Own",
    "quest.base.a_bed_of_your_own.why": "Until you sleep somewhere, death sends you back to world spawn. Two feathers and two hides make a sleeping bag, no table needed; wool and hide, or pelts, make one at Crafting 5. Junglefowl on warm grassland drop feathers, and rabbits in the grass drop hides.",
    "quest.base.the_potter": "The Potter",
    "quest.base.the_potter.why": "Pots and vials hold potions and stews, and the pot is the heart of the kiln you are working toward. Shape six clay pots from fired clay (five fired clay make two).",
    "quest.base.charcoal": "Charcoal",
    "quest.base.charcoal.why": "Fuel before metal: coal or charcoal smelts copper and makes torches. Burn logs down at a campfire (hold a log and right-click the fire), or dig out a coal seam: a small black-flecked stone on the ground marks one below.",
    "quest.base.red_metal": "Red Metal",
    "quest.base.red_metal.why": "Copper tools are faster and find more, and copper is three parts of bronze. A small copper-coloured stone on the ground marks a copper vein below it.",
    "quest.base.crucible_kiln": "Crucible Kiln",
    "quest.base.crucible_kiln.why": "Bronze needs heat a campfire can't reach. Lighting the kiln starts the Bronze age.",
    "quest.base.first_bronze": "First Bronze",
    "quest.base.first_bronze.why": "Smelt three copper ingots with one tin ore into bronze blend at the crafting table (Engineering 12), then put the blend in the lit kiln's crucible: the metal of the next age.",
    "block.base.pit_kiln": "Pit Kiln",
    "block.base.kiln_bricks": "Kiln Bricks",
    "block.base.crucible": "Crucible",
    "block.base.sleeping_bag": "Sleeping Bag",
    "block.base.clay_pot": "Clay Pot",
    "block.base.vial": "Vial",
    "block.base.bronze_blend": "Bronze Blend",
    "block.base.bronze_ingot": "Bronze Ingot",
    "multiblock.base.homestead_hearth": "Homestead Hearth",
    "multiblock.base.homestead_hearth.hint": "The hearth needs a ring of stone around the hearthstone and a chimney two blocks tall at one corner.",
    "multiblock.base.crucible_kiln": "Crucible Kiln",
    "multiblock.base.crucible_kiln.hint": "The kiln needs kiln bricks all round the crucible and a pillar of kiln bricks on each corner.",
    "quest.base.look_it_up": "Look It Up",
    "quest.base.look_it_up.why": "Forgotten a recipe? Open the inventory, type part of a name in its search box, and click the item to see how it is made; a right-click shows what it goes into. Look up the stone pickaxe.",
    "quest.base.first_night": "First Night",
    "quest.base.first_night.why": "Make a campfire: put two logs or Wood blocks above two Cobblestones in the 2×2 crafting grid. No stripped wood is needed. Place the fire, select raw rabbit, raw chicken or an egg in your hotbar, and right-click the fire. Rabbits and junglefowl roam open grassland; a junglefowl gives chicken and sometimes an egg. Wait two seconds; the cooked food goes into your inventory. If it burns, try again. Cooked food heals more than raw food.",
    "quest.base.stone_in_hand": "Stone in Hand",
    "quest.base.stone_in_hand.why": "Bare hands are slow. Stone tools mine twice as fast and reach coal for torches.",
    "quest.base.where_to_settle": "Where to Settle",
    "quest.base.where_to_settle.why": "Biomes help different work: the woods heal, the water fishes, the mountains mine. Walk until you have stood in three different ones; where you build decides what your home gives.",
    "quest.base.homestead_hearth": "Homestead Hearth",
    "quest.base.homestead_hearth.why": "Your home: you wake here after dying, and the Farm age opens. Craft a hearthstone (eight cobblestone round an empty middle) and two chimney blocks (six cobblestone and two clay each). Set the hearthstone in a ring of eight stone, stack both chimneys on one corner stone, then right-click the hearthstone. About 28 cobblestone and 4 clay in all; clay lies on the bottom of ponds and lakes, so wade in and dig it with a shovel.",
    "quest.base.a_friend_in_the_wild": "A Friend in the Wild",
    "quest.base.a_friend_in_the_wild.why": "Hold wheat seeds (or a carrot for a rabbit), walk up slowly without sprinting or hitting, and right-click a junglefowl. Junglefowl keep to warm grassland and jungle; rabbits to grassland and heath. A tamed hen lays eggs at home: your first step to a farm, and to pets.",
    "quest.base.bare_hands": "First Catch",
    "quest.base.bare_hands.why": "Fish are the easiest food near water. Hold your rod, right-click water and wait for a bite: shrimp and minnows come first. Land five; cooked fish heal well.",
    "quest.base.twine_and_thong": "Twine and Thong",
    "quest.base.twine_and_thong.why": "Twine goes into fishing rods, pouches, candles and baskets. Three wheat twist into two twine. Wild wheat grows as lone golden tufts on open grassland, a tuft every twenty blocks or so on plains, steppe and meadows, and a village's fields grow it too. Make ten.",
    "quest.base.pockets": "Pockets",
    "quest.base.pockets.why": "Herbs and seeds eat slots; a pouch holds a thousand of a kind in one.",
    "quest.base.torchlight": "Torchlight",
    "quest.base.torchlight.why": "Light keeps monsters off and lets you work at night.",
    "quest.base.crafting_table": "Crafting Table",
    "quest.base.crafting_table.why": "Its three-by-three grid makes every tool and weapon.",
    "quest.base.first_ore": "Red Metal Underfoot",
    "quest.base.first_ore.why": "Copper needs Mining 5 and the pickaxe you have. It lies in veins underground, mostly below sea level and richest under granite; a small copper-coloured stone lying on the ground marks a vein below it, so dig down there. Mine five; it is the start of every metal.",
    "quest.base.timber": "Timber",
    "quest.base.timber.why": "You start with nothing, and every tool starts as wood. Punch a tree trunk (hold the attack button: bare hands are slow, but they work) and gather eight logs; woods have the most trees, and plains have a few in groves. A log splits into four planks at the crafting grid; four planks make a crafting table, and with sticks (two planks make four) the table makes a wooden pickaxe and axe.",
    "quest.base.a_pile_of_stone": "A Pile of Stone",
    "quest.base.a_pile_of_stone.why": "Stone is the next step up from wood. It lies a few blocks under the dirt almost everywhere, and bare on cliffs, hillsides and mountains. Break twenty stone with your pickaxe: it drops cobblestone, which makes stone tools, a campfire and, later, your hearth.",
    "quest.base.coal_and_cinders": "Coal and Cinders",
    "quest.base.coal_and_cinders.why": "Coal shows as black flecks in the rock. It lies in wide seams around sea level and below, most often under limestone, sandstone and chalk; a small black-flecked stone lying on the ground marks a seam below it. One coal or charcoal over a stick makes four torches, and it smelts metal later. Mine eight.",
    "quest.base.something_to_swing": "Something to Swing",
    "quest.base.something_to_swing.why": "Fists are slow. A stone sword (two cobblestone over a stick) or a bone club (two bones over a stick) hits much harder; field mice in the grass, aurochs and wolves drop bones. Make one at the crafting table.",
    "quest.base.small_game": "Small Game",
    "quest.base.small_game.why": "Rabbits, junglefowl and other small animals are the easiest food: raw rabbit and chicken cook well at a campfire. Look for them on open grassland. Hunt three; a few blows are enough, and each kill trains Hunter. Then cook one of what you killed.",
    "quest.base.hide_and_seek": "Hide and Seek",
    "quest.base.hide_and_seek.why": "Hide makes armour, pouches and bedding. Rabbits on grassland drop it, and so do deer and boar in the woods; a knife in your hand makes it drop more often. Gather four hides, and keep two bones as well: field mice in the grass drop them, and a bone makes a club, a needle, a handle.",
    "quest.base.hide_wraps": "Hide Wraps",
    "quest.base.hide_wraps.why": "Armour turns blows aside and trains Defence. Hide gloves (two hide) and boots (three hide) are the cheapest pieces. Make both at the crafting table.",
    "quest.base.meat_and_fire": "Meat on the Fire",
    "quest.base.meat_and_fire.why": "Raw meat heals little and leaves you Queasy; cooked meat heals far more. Cook six pieces of meat at a campfire: rabbit, chicken, duck or frog. Ducks and frogs live by rivers and in swamps. A higher Cooking level burns less. Six good meals will also take you to Cooking 2.",
    "quest.base.a_handful_of_grain": "A Handful of Grain",
    "quest.base.a_handful_of_grain.why": "Wild wheat grows as lone golden tufts on open grassland: look on plains, steppe and meadows, where there is a tuft every twenty blocks or so, or break the wheat in a village's fields. Break it for seeds and the odd ear of wheat: wheat makes bread and twine, and the seeds are your first crop.",
    "quest.base.daily_bread": "Daily Bread",
    "quest.base.daily_bread.why": "Two ears of wheat side by side in the crafting grid bake into bread, which heals more than the grain. Bake four loaves.",
    "quest.base.break_ground": "Break Ground",
    "quest.base.break_ground.why": "A hoe tills grass or dirt into farmland, where seeds can be sown. Make a hoe at the crafting table: two stone or two planks over two sticks. Right-click soil with it to till.",
    "quest.base.rod_and_line": "Rod and Line",
    "quest.base.rod_and_line.why": "A fishing rod is three sticks and two twine, laid out at the crafting table as the recipe shows. Twine is three wheat twisted into two. With the rod in hand, right-click water and wait for a bite. Then land one fish.",
    "quest.base.a_fish_supper": "A Fish Supper",
    "quest.base.a_fish_supper.why": "A fish tastes far better cooked. Roast three at a campfire: hold the raw fish and right-click the fire. Catch the three yourself.",
    "quest.base.wild_harvest": "Wild Harvest",
    "quest.base.wild_harvest.why": "The wild gives herbs, flowers, berries and mushrooms for the picking. Pick five different kinds by hand; most grow back in time. Flowers and herbs crowd flower meadows, berry bushes and mushrooms grow in the woods, and raspberries in meadows. Your journal's Plants page records each kind you pick.",
    "quest.base.herb_gatherer": "Herb Gatherer",
    "quest.base.herb_gatherer.why": "Herbs flavour food, heal and brew into potions later. Pick five herbs: flower meadows are full of chamomile, sorrel and yarrow, mint grows by water, and sage and thyme on warm, dry ground. Carry them in a herb pouch so they do not eat your slots.",
    "quest.base.neighbours": "Wild Neighbours",
    "quest.base.neighbours.why": "Walk the land and meet who lives in it. Get right up close to six kinds of animal, within three blocks with nothing in between: rabbits and junglefowl on grassland, deer and boar in the woods, ducks by water. The journal's Animals page fills in as you go, and every kind drops something different.",
    "quest.base.lay_of_the_land": "Lay of the Land",
    "quest.base.lay_of_the_land.why": "Before you settle, see more of the world. Stand in six different biomes: woods, plains, hills, wetlands and shores each hold different animals, plants and ores.",
    "quest.base.something_hostile": "Something Hostile",
    "quest.base.something_hostile.why": "Not everything out there is food. Cave bats and cave crawlers lurk in the dark underground, and shamblers walk where the aether is strong. Fight one with a sword in hand and torches and bread at your belt.",
    "quest.base.sharpening_up": "Sharpening Up",
    "quest.base.sharpening_up.why": "Every blow you land trains Attack, and a higher level hits harder and truer. Hunt until you reach Attack 4. Five kills along the way.",
    "quest.base.raise_your_guard": "Raise Your Guard",
    "quest.base.raise_your_guard.why": "A shield blocks blows: right-click to raise your guard as a swing lands. A hide buckler (four hide and a stick) is the easy one; a wooden shield (planks) needs Crafting 3.",
    "quest.base.tools_for_animals": "Tools for Animals",
    "quest.base.tools_for_animals.why": "Shears take wool from sheep and a pail takes milk from cows and goats. Two cobblestones crossed make shears; two planks crossed make a pail.",
    "quest.base.a_sharp_edge": "A Sharp Edge",
    "quest.base.a_sharp_edge.why": "A knife is the hunter's tool: it makes a kill drop hide more often and cuts plants cleanly. A wooden knife is a plank over a stick, a stone knife a cobblestone over a stick; both fit the inventory grid.",
    "quest.base.clay_banks": "Clay Banks",
    "quest.base.clay_banks.why": "Pots, vials and kiln bricks are all clay. It lies in patches on the bottom of ponds, lakes and rivers: wade in and dig it with a shovel (one cobblestone over two sticks). Carry out twenty-four.",
    "quest.base.a_pit_kiln": "A Pit Kiln",
    "quest.base.a_pit_kiln.why": "Clay needs more heat than an open fire gives. A pit kiln is a campfire ringed with cobblestone: lay five cobblestones round a campfire at the crafting table, as the recipe shows, then set it down.",
    "quest.base.fire_the_clay": "Fire the Clay",
    "quest.base.fire_the_clay.why": "Hold clay and right-click the pit kiln: after a moment it comes out as fired clay. Low Crafting levels crack some, so bring spare. Fire twelve.",
    "quest.base.brick_by_brick": "Brick by Brick",
    "quest.base.brick_by_brick.why": "The Crucible Kiln is built of kiln bricks: nineteen for the kiln and its crucible. Four fired clay make a brick at the crafting grid (Crafting 5). Make nineteen; it is a lot of clay, so keep firing.",
    "quest.base.the_crucible": "The Crucible",
    "quest.base.the_crucible.why": "The heart of the kiln: seven kiln bricks round a clay pot, shaped at the crafting table (Engineering 10). Make it, then build the kiln round it.",
    "quest.base.first_harvest": "First Harvest",
    "quest.base.first_harvest.why": "Till grass or dirt with a hoe (right-click), sow wheat seeds on the farmland (right-click), keep water within four blocks, and wait: wheat ripens in about twelve minutes. Break the ripe plants to harvest. Harvest four. Keep the four wheat you harvest in your pack.",
    "quest.base.a_field_of_gold": "A Field of Gold",
    "quest.base.a_field_of_gold.why": "One plot is a hobby; a field is a food supply. Keep sowing from your own seed and harvest twenty-four wheat plants. Seeds come back with each harvest, so the field pays for itself. A field that size also teaches Farming 4.",
    "quest.base.carrot_patch": "Carrot Patch",
    "quest.base.carrot_patch.why": "Carrots need Farming 5 and cool, moist soil. A carrot is its own seed: forage wild carrots (white-flowered, thickest in flower meadows, a few on plains), plant what you get, and harvest four. Rabbits love them too. Keep the four carrots you harvest.",
    "quest.base.herb_garden": "Herb Garden",
    "quest.base.herb_garden.why": "Herbs cannot be sown, but a herb planter (planks round dirt, Construction 3) lets a picked herb grow back at home. Make a planter, set a herb in it, and pick it again when it returns. Pick six wild plants on your rounds as well.",
    "quest.base.camp_cook": "Camp Cook",
    "quest.base.camp_cook.why": "Every dish trains Cooking. Duck wants level 3, mutton 5 and crab 6, and a higher level burns less. Cook a mix of meat and fish, whatever your hunting and fishing bring, until you reach Cooking 5.",
    "quest.base.seed_mix": "Seed Mix",
    "quest.base.seed_mix.why": "Kept animals only breed when fed their breeding food. Two seeds and a wheat in the crafting grid make seed mix (Cooking 8), which readies any kept animal to breed. Make four. Bring in eight wheat to make it from.",
    "quest.base.roots_in_the_embers": "Roots in the Embers",
    "quest.base.roots_in_the_embers.why": "A roast carrot heals better than a raw one, and roots are easy food to grow. Roast four carrots on a campfire (Cooking 2).",
    "quest.base.hens_in_a_row": "Hens in a Row",
    "quest.base.hens_in_a_row.why": "Hold wheat seeds, walk up slowly (no sprinting, no hitting) and right-click a junglefowl until it trusts you; they keep to warm grassland and jungle. A kept hen needs room, grass or feed, and water nearby, and lays an egg about every five minutes. Tame three.",
    "quest.base.fresh_eggs": "Fresh Eggs",
    "quest.base.fresh_eggs.why": "A kept hen lays on the ground near her, and a hen that is fed, watered and sheltered lays more. Fry your first egg on a campfire to taste the reward, then collect five more and keep them.",
    "quest.base.a_proper_breakfast": "A Proper Breakfast",
    "quest.base.a_proper_breakfast.why": "A fried egg is the quickest cooking there is: hold an egg and right-click a campfire. Fry three.",
    "quest.base.a_woolly_flock": "A Woolly Flock",
    "quest.base.a_woolly_flock.why": "Mouflon, the wild sheep, need Hunter 5 to tame; look on mountains and heath. Hold its favourite food, approach calmly and right-click. A kept sheep grows its wool back: shear it with your shears. Have your shears made before you go.",
    "quest.base.wool_gathering": "Wool Gathering",
    "quest.base.wool_gathering.why": "Wool makes beds, cloth and sleeping bags. Right-click a kept sheep with shears in hand whenever its wool has grown back, and gather six.",
    "quest.base.ducks_on_the_pond": "Ducks on the Pond",
    "quest.base.ducks_on_the_pond.why": "Mallards need Hunter 3, lay eggs, and do not mind rain. Hold its favourite food, approach one by the water and right-click.",
    "quest.base.the_milk_pail": "The Milk Pail",
    "quest.base.the_milk_pail.why": "A tamed mountain goat (Hunter 8), reindeer (10) or aurochs (12) gives milk to a pail, right-clicked. Goats live on mountains, reindeer on tundra and in taiga, aurochs on plains. Milk heals half as fast again for a while. Collect two. Make the pail first: two planks crossed.",
    "quest.base.a_full_pen": "A Full Pen",
    "quest.base.a_full_pen.why": "Six animals under your care is a real farm. Keep each fed, watered, roofed against rain and given room; condition decides what they give. You can keep up to 64 animals.",
    "quest.base.bigger_game": "Bigger Game",
    "quest.base.bigger_game.why": "Sheep, deer, boar and cattle give more meat and better hides, but they fight back: wear your hide wraps and keep your sword sharp. Deer and boar keep to the woods, aurochs to the plains, mouflon to the mountains. Cook the haunch: mutton at Cooking 5, pork at 8, venison at 15.",
    "quest.base.full_hide_wraps": "Full Hide Wraps",
    "quest.base.full_hide_wraps.why": "A whole set guards head, body and legs. At the crafting table a hood takes five hides, a tunic eight and trousers seven.",
    "quest.base.copper_arms": "Copper Arms",
    "quest.base.copper_arms.why": "Copper hits harder and lasts longer than stone. Smelt ingots (ore over charcoal in the grid, Engineering 5), then make a copper sword (two ingots over a stick) and a copper shield.",
    "quest.base.copper_mail": "Copper Mail",
    "quest.base.copper_mail.why": "A copper helmet takes five ingots and a chestplate eight. They turn aside far more than hide does, and every ingot is ore you carried out of the hills.",
    "quest.base.seasoned_fighter": "Seasoned Fighter",
    "quest.base.seasoned_fighter.why": "Bigger animals and tougher monsters teach Attack faster. Keep fighting until you reach Attack 8; your health grows with Hitpoints as you go.",
    "quest.base.tin_find": "A Silvery Ore",
    "quest.base.tin_find.why": "Tin is the other half of bronze. It needs Mining 10 and a pickaxe, so keep digging coal and copper to get there. Tin lies in the lower part of copper veins: where you found copper, dig below it. Mine three tin ore. Take three copper from the same seam: bronze wants both.",
    "quest.base.rock_collector": "Rock Collector",
    "quest.base.rock_collector.why": "Stone comes in many kinds, each with its own ore. The rock underfoot changes every few kilometres (granite, limestone, basalt, sandstone, slate), so dig down in different lands. Break six different rocks and ores, and your journal's Ores page fills in.",
    "quest.base.patient_angler": "Patient Angler",
    "quest.base.patient_angler.why": "Every catch trains Fishing, and the bigger fish bite only at higher levels. Fish until you reach Fishing 5, when sardines start biting in the sea.",
    "quest.base.many_kinds": "Many Kinds of Fish",
    "quest.base.many_kinds.why": "Rivers, lakes and the sea bite differently: shrimp anywhere, minnows in fresh water, sardines in the sea, perch in lakes from Fishing 10. Land three different kinds. Cook six of your catch: the best fish are worth a fire.",
    "quest.base.far_horizons": "Far Horizons",
    "quest.base.far_horizons.why": "The world is big and each biome has its own animals, plants and ores. Stand in twelve different biomes.",
    "quest.base.field_guide": "Field Guide",
    "quest.base.field_guide.why": "Get right up close to fifteen kinds of animal, within three blocks with nothing in between. The journal's Animals page records each one, and what it drops once you have hunted it.",
    "quest.base.a_seat_by_the_fire": "A Seat by the Fire",
    "quest.base.a_seat_by_the_fire.why": "A home needs somewhere to sit. A stool is two planks over two sticks (Construction 1); benches and chairs follow. Make two seats and set them by the hearth.",
    "quest.base.a_table_for_two": "A Table for Two",
    "quest.base.a_table_for_two.why": "Planks on four sticks make a table (Construction 3). Set it near the hearth with a seat on each side; a roof and a table make a house a home.",
    "quest.base.shelves_and_cupboards": "Shelves and Cupboards",
    "quest.base.shelves_and_cupboards.why": "Somewhere to put things: a shelf (Construction 4) and a cupboard (Construction 6), both from planks at the crafting table. Make one of each.",
    "quest.base.a_proper_bed": "A Proper Bed",
    "quest.base.a_proper_bed.why": "Sleep on something better than the ground: three wool over three planks (Construction 5). Place it in your home and right-click to sleep.",
    "quest.base.wool_and_dye": "Wool and Dye",
    "quest.base.wool_and_dye.why": "A cloth is a wool and a flower of the colour you want, side by side in the grid (Crafting 2): white from a daisy, yellow from a dandelion, red from a poppy. Daisies grow on plains, dandelions in flower meadows, poppies on the steppe. Make two.",
    "quest.base.a_rug_underfoot": "A Rug Underfoot",
    "quest.base.a_rug_underfoot.why": "Two cloths side by side make three rugs (Crafting 3). Lay them on the floor; curtains, cushions and banners are made from cloth too.",
    "quest.base.earthenware": "Earthenware",
    "quest.base.earthenware.why": "Fired clay makes plates, bowls, jars and jugs for the shelf, and a basket is twine. Make three pieces of crockery at the crafting table.",
    "quest.base.candlelight": "Candlelight",
    "quest.base.candlelight.why": "Twine and two hides make two candles (Crafting 3): a softer light than a torch for a table or shelf.",
    "quest.base.food_enough": "Food Enough",
    "quest.base.food_enough.why": "Food that lasts is a farm that works. Show any one: harvest twelve wheat and six carrots or rye, keep four animals well fed and housed (condition at least 75), or land forty fish. Ten loaves of bread are your reward.",
    "quest.base.full_stone_kit": "A Full Stone Kit",
    "quest.base.full_stone_kit.why": "A stone tool works twice as fast as a wooden one and finds a little more. Carry the whole kit: pickaxe, axe, shovel (one cobblestone over two sticks), hoe and knife.",
    "quest.base.dig_in": "Dig In",
    "quest.base.dig_in.why": "The hearth needs four clay, and clay lies on the bottom of ponds and lakes. A stone shovel digs four times faster than bare hands: make one, wade in and dig four.",
    "quest.base.stockpile": "Stockpile",
    "quest.base.stockpile.why": "A home runs on common stock. Carry thirty-two logs and sixty-four cobblestone and nothing you want to build is a trip away. Woods give the logs fastest, and stone lies a few blocks under the dirt almost anywhere.",
    "quest.base.copper_kit": "Copper Kit",
    "quest.base.copper_kit.why": "Copper works six times as fast as a bare hand, a step above stone, and finds more. An axe takes three ingots, a shovel one, a hoe two and a knife one: seven in all.",
    "quest.base.make_camp": "Make Camp",
    "quest.base.make_camp.why": "A camp is a bed and a light together. Put your sleeping bag down, set a torch beside it and sleep in it once: wherever you wake is your home, and a camp heals you a fifth faster.",
    "quest.base.snug_for_winter": "Snug for Winter",
    "quest.base.snug_for_winter.why": "Put a roof over the Hearth with your bed and two lights beside it, and the home turns snug: warm under a roof, you heal half as fast again there, and a night's sleep in it rests you better.",
    "quest.base.workshop_and_stove": "A Stove and a Quern",
    "quest.base.workshop_and_stove.why": "A home that works for you. A stove is a campfire ringed with six cobblestones (Construction 5); a quern, spindle or loom gives your hands something to do by the fire (Crafting 5 to 8).",
    "quest.base.books_and_banners": "Books and Banners",
    "quest.base.books_and_banners.why": "A bookshelf (planks and hides, Construction 8) and a banner (cloth and a stick, Crafting 5) say whose home this is. Make one of each.",
    "quest.base.a_homely_home": "A Homely Home",
    "quest.base.a_homely_home.why": "Room to sit, work and store: two seats, a table, two places to keep things and a third light under the roof. A homely home helps you learn a twentieth faster.",
    "quest.base.a_cosy_home": "A Cosy Home",
    "quest.base.a_cosy_home.why": "Soft and bright: two rugs, two curtains, a cushion, three pieces of crockery and a fourth light. A cosy home heals you faster and teaches a tenth more, and a night in it is a deep rest.",
    "quest.base.heart_of_the_home": "Heart of the Home",
    "quest.base.heart_of_the_home.why": "Everything a home needs: a bookshelf, a stove or cauldron, a quern, spindle or loom, and a banner, all in a cosy home. Heal twice as fast and learn an eighth more where you live.",
    "quest.base.ore_run": "An Ore Run",
    "quest.base.ore_run.why": "Bronze needs a good store of ore. With a copper kit you dig fast: bring up twenty-four copper, nine tin and twelve coal, and the crucible will not wait on you. Copper lies below sea level with tin in the lower part of the same vein, coal in seams near sea level; small copper and coal stones lying on the ground mark the veins below.",
